WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.810
Tomorrow, at 10:00 AM Japanese Standard Time,

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.730
the Midsummer's Knights will return with the Engine series to Tanegashima,

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.530
aboard the container capsule <i>Flügel</i>.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.530
Only one day, eh?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.830
We've got to get close to him while we have the chance.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:18.740
Come on...

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.410
We're in your hands.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.960
Hana, Pitz is doing much better.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.250
Pitz!

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.840
Thank you for taking care of Pitz, Akari.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.300
Don't be silly.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.720
Friends help each other out when they can, isn't that right?

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.140
Friends?

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.060
We've nearly finished laying the groundwork for this operation.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.270
Sending Mutou Hana back to Earth will be risky.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.030
I realize that.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.950
Daichi and Teppei have been left there for just that reason.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.950
I'd like you two to protect Hana.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.200
Roger.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.580
But...

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.490
It's okay.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.500
If I'm with these two, I'll be fine.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:13.210
Plan B should have advanced to phase 2 preparations by the time they return.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.760
Arashi Teppei's test has been completed.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.720
The only one left is Manatsu Daichi.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.390
I'm ready.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:29.360
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:36.530
I'm watching an endless dream

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:42.990
Aren't you watching too?

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.340
It's always close by no matter how far away it seems

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:57.180
Can't you see it too?

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.640
The things you can't normally say

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.350
The things you try to express

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.850
The things you're willing to fight for

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:13.570
Standing on your own two feet

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:20.240
The night sky illuminates them all

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:27.370
The first flash of lightning

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:33.710
This is our battle to fight

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:41.050
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:49.560
This dream will absolutely come true

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.400
The Earth Engine Impactor has arrived at the testing area within Sigma sector.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.990
Unit will remain on standby.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.780
Orgone spectrometer, calorimeter,

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.740
and other observational instruments are all transmitting clearly.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:06.950
Ready any time.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.460
Captain, we're ready here.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:11.790
Roger.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:15.920
Here I go.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.480
How does it look?

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.310
Maximum output is 1.7 gigajoules.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.020
Teppei's output is a bit higher.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:39.530
Though it's still only 1.8 gigajoules.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:46.530
2 gigajoules is the bare minimum required to fire the boosted plasmagnum.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.040
In live combat, Teppei's maximum output has been as high as 2.2,

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.920
and the captain has also produced up to 2.1 gigajoules.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.880
The fact that their levels haven't stabilized is our greatest concern.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:02.340
But... the success of this operation hinges on them, doesn't it?

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.640
Onslaught Through
the Wilderness

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:32.370
Hey, is it true you don't have a girlfriend?

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.330
Yeah.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.830
Do you have a girl you like?

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.630
I don't know.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.840
Does he, I wonder...

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.470
What do you think?

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:48.720
Come in.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.190
Thanks for coming.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.650
Do you need something, Governor?

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.830
Hello.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.130
Do you know anything about <i>Kivotos</i>?

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:25.880
Isn't it a spaceship?

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:31.850
I called you here to ask a personal question.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:38.100
I suppose I'm interested in you...

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.110
Interested?

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.190
Because I'm not a normal person?

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.280
No, that's not why.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.660
It's because Akari called you her friend.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.450
Even when she was little she had a hard time making friends.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.870
Maybe it was out of stubbornness.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.170
But you're the first person I've ever heard her call a friend.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.380
Akari is my friend!

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:09.840
Thank you.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:11.970
I'm happy to hear that.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:13.810
Why?

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.390
Because I'm her mother... I suppose.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:23.820
Sometimes, I think Akari doesn't need me.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.940
Did Akari say that?

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.820
It only makes sense that she'd feel that way.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.120
I've left her alone for a very long time.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.120
I've only been her mother when it was convenient for me.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.340
Akari isn't the kind of girl to think that way.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.050
I don't have a family...

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.050
But I have Akari, Teppei, and Daichi.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.350
I'm really happy.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.180
But when I see you,

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:59.390
I think having a real family must be nice, too.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.270
Why?

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:08.360
Because whenever you talk about Akari, you look so kind.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:20.410
I'm sorry.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.420
Can I stay like this a little longer?

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.180
This is what a mom smells like, huh?

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.140
Listen, Hana...

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:46.070
<i>Kivotos</i> will only be able to fulfill its true mission

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.820
after docking with another spaceship.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.660
This ship is humanity's last hope for survival.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.790
I'm Professor Canis.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:03.120
I played a large role in the development of <i>Kivotos</i>.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:04.960
And you are?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.340
Manatsu Daichi.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:11.010
I've heard that name before.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:13.840
Ah...

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.600
Then, you're the captain of the Midsummer's Knights?

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:24.020
What an honor it is to meet a hero here.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.770
I'm not a hero.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.280
I won't have this chance again.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:33.490
Please shake my hand.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.240
Rechecking the return trajectory to Tanegashima.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:41.830
All three ordinaries are mounted in the container.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:46.500
Let's make sure to go swimming again the next time you're up here, Teppei!

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:47.840
Roger.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.710
You're popular, Teppei!

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.680
Hana, give Akari my regards.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:56.890
Roger.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.770
You seem different, somehow.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.440
What's wrong, Captain?

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.270
A scientist I met here shook my hand.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.230
Shook your hand?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:21.790
So this is the chosen hero's hand.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:28.290
He said my hand was "the chosen hero's hand."

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:32.380
But I'm not a hero.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.140
That's right.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.350
You're no hero.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:47.310
You're merely a child who
happened to get a Livlaster.

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:51.480
You're about to realize that.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.280
Return program is now entering final sequence.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.080
Shutting down primary thruster.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.790
The deceleration thrusters stopped two seconds earlier than expected.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:14.000
Recalculated trajectory indicates no problems with atmospheric reentry.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.470
But we will land a good distance away from the original point.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.470
What does this mean?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.930
The <i>Flügel</i> has entered the atmosphere.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.020
Tracing estimated course...

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.730
I have their landing point.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.690
It's in Australia.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.780
They got us.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.650
A spy?

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:41.620
The <i>Tenkaido's</i> crew numbers in the hundreds.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.120
Some are bound to be Ark Faction extremists.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.830
The return program was altered?

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.540
If this is the Ark Faction's doing,
they must be after Hana!

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.420
The <i>Flügel</i> has crash-landed!

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:59.470
Southeast Australia, area 6!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.010
The desert?

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:02.220
Can we contact the <i>Flügel</i>?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.010
This is Tanegashima!

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:05.310
Do you copy, <i>Flügel</i>?

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.100
This is Manatsu.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.770
We've crash-landed successfully.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.100
No one's hurt.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:13.020
We will now...

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:16.690
What's wrong, Daichi?

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.450
We've lost communication with the <i>Flügel</i>!

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.820
An aurora storm is occurring!

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.070
Electromagnetic fluctuations are scrambling our communications.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.660
That solar flare has reached Earth, then?

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:32.000
The enemy's plans even accounted for that?

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.630
I lost contact with the base.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:41.430
Close-range communications like this work fine.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.470
They deliberately sent us here?

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:47.770
Australian Central Command is nearby.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.730
We should assume this is all a trap by the enemy.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:55.440
It's okay.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.570
We'll get home safely.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.400
I'm counting on you, Livlaster.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.580
By mastering the Livlaster's use,

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:18.550
it should ultimately be possible to generate nigh infinite amounts of energy.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.260
Of course, they haven't mastered it yet.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.180
Their output is limited.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:30.270
But the Princess's Livlaster used ecdysis mode.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:35.230
There's a good chance it will become even more powerful.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:39.820
Why can't we Planetary Gears fire the Livlaster?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.490
I can find no logical answer to that question.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:46.200
But reports from Globe scientists say

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:53.000
they believe the Livlasters are extradimensional life forms that choose to manifest as guns.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.380
They just aren't compatible with us, then?

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:03.340
Come to think of it, Kube got dumped by Hitomi.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.220
Can you keep him under control?

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:11.850
I've received no information that would indicate Makino Hitomi has dumped Kube Masaki.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.400
What more "information" do you need?

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.900
He's gone after every girl in the company.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.540
Hitomi won't be able to take it.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:36.250
He's like a monkey in heat.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:38.670
A monkey?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.960
Calm down, Pitz.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:47.630
I'll get Hana and the others back with my magic.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.430
Wait, maybe...

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.390
Is Hana in danger?

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:56.480
I brought them down as planned.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:58.980
Now pluck the flower.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:00.940
Over.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:04.940
Eyecatch

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.910
It may be winter in the Southern hemisphere, but it isn't particularly cold.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:14.620
Come to think of it, this is the first time I've even been in another country.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.250
But you're in space all the time.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.540
Should space count as another country...?

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.760
Hey, Teppei...

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.510
What are you eating over there?

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.260
The girls on the <i>Tenkaido</i> made it for me.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.270
You're so popular, Teppei!

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.430
You really are...

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:44.530
Nothing like me, a guy whose first overseas trip was the result of an accidental crash-landing.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.280
Have you not traveled a lot, Daichi?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:53.910
I guess the farthest I've traveled is to Tanegashima with my dad when I was little.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.910
What were your mom and dad like, Daichi?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.250
I never told you?

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.210
My dad was a Globe space pilot!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:09.630
I think he died fighting the first Kill-T-Gang that attacked Earth.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:14.600
Parents are kind of mysterious, aren't they?

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:19.940
What about your mom?

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:24.650
My mom died of an illness when I was little.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:28.440
So my uncle raised me.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:32.110
You don't remember your mom?

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.540
No, not really...

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.200
But why?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.920
No reason.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:46.920
The enemy?

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.520
They aren't friends.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:06.150
It seems likely that they're with whoever forced our landing here.

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.190
Oh, look.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.110
A message from the enemy.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.410
"Disarm and surrender."

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:14.490
How should we respond?

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:15.660
No need to respond.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.200
We're leaving.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:20.370
It's coming back.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.000
Guess it'll be hard to escape them...

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.080
Teppei?

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.090
Teppei!

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.260
Hey, Teppei!

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.930
We shouldn't fight if we don't have to...

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.140
It's a UCAV, Captain.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.520
And one of Globe's.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.690
The Ark Faction?

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.900
Hey, Captain...

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:47.730
What?

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.150
Even if someone were piloting it,

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:52.440
I'd shoot them for the team's sake.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:57.030
The time will come when you'll be forced to make that choice.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:58.830
You know that, right?

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:01.450
But, well...

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:05.040
These days, there aren't many manned weapons.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.050
Let's hurry.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.680
This isn't the end, is it?

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:21.100
If it's the Ark Faction, they'll keep coming until they get Hana

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:22.470
because she controls the <i>Blume</i>.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:25.690
Artillery fire from 3 o'clock!

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.610
I knew it. They're here.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.770
Ahead of us, Captain!

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.620
We've been ambushed.

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:40.450
Yeah.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.420
They've sent the tank brigade.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.790
And they have us so thoroughly surrounded.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.130
These are unmanned, too.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.300
Roger!

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.270
They're only attacking the Earth and the Nebula.

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.020
I get it

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:13.480
That UCAV was to see which one Hana's piloting!

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:15.940
Which means...

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:19.070
You and I will be killed here, Captain.

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:20.280
Seriously?

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:24.910
Captain, above you!

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:35.510
People on Earth are scarier than <i>those</i> guys even!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:39.180
It makes you wonder about the people we're protecting, doesn't it?

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.270
Teppei!

00:18:58.780 --> 00:18:59.860
Teppei!

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:00.950
Teppei!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:14.500
Captain, the Nebula Engine is down.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:15.500
I can't move.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.090
Take Hana and run!

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:22.590
If they're here to capture me, they won't attack me, and I can protect you both.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.850
Getting out of here isn't our only mission.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:30.060
Isn't returning Hana safely to Tanegashima our mission?

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:34.770
Once the smoke clears, they'll attack us all at once!

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:39.900
Before that happens, leave me and go, Captain!

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:51.580
So this is the chosen hero's hand.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:57.380
He said my hand was "the chosen hero's hand."

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.920
But I'm not a hero.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:04.260
You weren't chosen by fate.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:08.060
You chose everything of your own free will,

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:12.230
and you can grasp everything with that hand.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:14.310
Right?

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.870
What's wrong, Captain?

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.380
Captain!

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:41.590
Can I grasp it?

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.050
No, I will grasp it!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:08.870
Wow.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.840
Why didn't you leave me and run?

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.390
Wouldn't you have done the same thing?

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.890
You're being naïve, Captain.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:35.480
If you keep that up, you'll lose something really important someday.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:40.940
But thank you for saving me.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:45.200
That attack was amazing.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.990
What kind of output did you get?

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:48.990
Output?

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.410
5.8 gigajoules?

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:57.620
5.8 gigajoules?

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.670
I'm amazed, Captain.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:04.420
Teppei, is the Nebula okay?

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:07.260
It doesn't look like it will explode or anything.

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:10.430
But it can't walk on its own.

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:13.100
The two of us can carry the Nebula, right?

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:17.060
For now, let's get to Australia Central Command.

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:20.360
If we can get that far, it'll probably be fine.

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:29.360
The Midsummer's Knights are heading for Central Command.

00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:33.830
It's time to put the flower back in her vase.

00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:37.750
Make sure you capture Mutou Hana.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:42.000
For the sake of humanity's future.

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:16.930
We "borrow" a large transport plane from Globe's Carpentaria base,

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:20.520
and set a course for Tanegashima.

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:25.020
But more new weapons from Salty Dog attack us.

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:28.070
This one's kind of bad!

00:24:28.070 --> 00:24:30.530
Just then, right in front of us is...

00:24:30.530 --> 00:24:33.490
Next time, on episode 19 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:33.490 --> 00:24:35.570
Your Smile Means Everything

00:24:33.910 --> 00:24:35.570
Your Smile Means Everything.

00:24:35.570 --> 00:24:38.490
Earth Engine, expand!
